-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> Hence, the Hadamard product in expression III is well-defined.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".</p>\n</div></div>",
